{"call_id":"call_6dDdGmutymBBc4DzwtAUQH9E","process_id":"63168","turn_id":"019c9e63-d35d-7332-a538-c4c383caa5ac","command":["/usr/bin/bash","-lc","kspec task get @01KJF687"],"cwd":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec task get @01KJF687"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"Ralph: Stream terminal/run output to session files and return bounded previews\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KJF687QGPXXV00F9ZPTQJKYF\nType:      bug\nStatus:    pending\nPriority:  1\nAutomation: eligible\n\n─── Description ───\n  Problem: terminal/run currently accumulates child stdout/stderr in unbounded in-memory strings, which can OOM long codex runs.\n  \n  Scope (steps 1-2):\n  1) In terminal/run handler, stream stdout/stderr directly to per-session files (e.g., .kspec/sessions/<id>/tool-output/<toolCallId>.stdout.log and .stderr.log).\n  2) Keep only bounded in-memory preview (e.g., first N chars/lines and byte counters) for tool response + CLI display.\n  3) Include metadata in tool response: stdout_path, stderr_path, stdout_bytes, stderr_bytes, preview_truncated.\n  4) Preserve current UX by showing truncated preview in CLI while retaining full output on disk.\n  \n  Done when: reproducing command-heavy codex run no longer grows heap unbounded from terminal/run output, and full output is still retrievable from session artifacts.\nSpec ref:  @cli-ralph\nTags:      ralph, memory, session-log\nCreated:   2026-02-27T09:18:07.599Z\n\n─── Spec Context ───\nRalph command - automated task loop\nType: feature\nImplementation: implemented\nDescription:\n  Automated task loop using ACP protocol. Runs claude-agent-acp agent in a loop to process kspec tasks autonomously with full event logging and streaming output.\nAcceptance Criteria:\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: ready tasks exist\n    When: kspec ralph is run with --max-loops N\n    Then: spawns ACP agent and runs up to N iterations\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: no ready tasks exist\n    When: kspec ralph is run\n    Then: command exits with message indicating no ready tasks\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: a loop iteration starts\n    When: agent picks and works on a task\n    Then: agent uses task start, task note, and task complete commands per working procedure\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: a loop iteration ends with work still in progress\n    When: agent cannot complete the task in one iteration\n    Then: agent commits WIP, adds note documenting progress, and task remains in_progress for next iteration\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: a loop iteration completes (task done or WIP)\n    When: there are uncommitted changes\n    Then: agent commits the changes with appropriate message\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: --dry-run flag is provided\n    When: kspec ralph --dry-run is run\n    Then: shows the prompt that would be sent without executing agent\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: agent returns error during iteration\n    When: the error occurs\n    Then: retry the iteration up to max-retries times before failing the loop\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: multiple consecutive iterations fail after all retries\n    When: the failure count reaches max-failures threshold\n    Then: the loop exits early with an error message\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: --adapter flag is provided\n    When: kspec ralph --adapter <id> is run\n    Then: uses specified adapter (default claude-agent-acp)\n  [ac-10]\n    Given: session starts\n    When: agent spawns\n    Then: creates new session with ULID and logs session.start event\n  [ac-11]\n    Given: agent streams updates\n    When: updates arrive\n    Then: displays streaming output to CLI and logs to session events\n  [ac-12]\n    Given: prompt is sent\n    When: iteration starts\n    Then: logs prompt.sent event with full prompt content\n  [ac-13]\n    Given: session ends\n    When: loop completes or errors\n    Then: logs session.end event with status and triggers commit\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: a loop iteration starts\n    When: building prompt for the agent\n    Then: creates a fresh ACP session so each iteration has a clean context window\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: --focus flag is provided with instructions\n    When: building prompt for each iteration\n    Then: includes the focus instructions prominently in the prompt, emphasizing they apply to all iterations\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: ralph loop is running\n    When: checking for available tasks (ready or in_progress)\n    Then: only considers tasks with automation: eligible status; both ready tasks and in_progress tasks are filtered by automation eligibility\n  [ac-17]\n    Given: ralph loop is running with --restart-every N (N > 0)\n    When: iteration completes and iteration number is divisible by N\n    Then: agent process is killed and respawned to prevent memory buildup\n  [ac-18]\n    Given: --restart-every 0 is specified\n    When: iterations complete\n    Then: agent process is never restarted (maintains single agent instance)\n  [ac-19]\n    Given: ralph loop iteration completes\n    When: determining whether to continue looping\n    Then: loop continues if automation:eligible ready tasks OR automation:eligible in_progress tasks exist; exits with message when neither remain\n  [ac-20]\n    Given: processPendingReviewTasks completes during iteration\n    When: checking for loop continuation\n    Then: uses freshly gathered task context (not stale from iteration start) to detect tasks that became ready due to dependency unblocking\n  [ac-21]\n    Given: User runs kspec ralph with --tasks @ref1,@ref2\n    When: task selection runs each iteration\n    Then: only the explicitly listed tasks are considered for work, regardless of automation eligibility of other tasks; exits when all listed tasks are completed or blocked\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Ralph: Stream terminal/run output to session files and return bounded previews\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KJF687QGPXXV00F9ZPTQJKYF\nType:      bug\nStatus:    pending\nPriority:  1\nAutomation: eligible\n\n─── Description ───\n  Problem: terminal/run currently accumulates child stdout/stderr in unbounded in-memory strings, which can OOM long codex runs.\n  \n  Scope (steps 1-2):\n  1) In terminal/run handler, stream stdout/stderr directly to per-session files (e.g., .kspec/sessions/<id>/tool-output/<toolCallId>.stdout.log and .stderr.log).\n  2) Keep only bounded in-memory preview (e.g., first N chars/lines and byte counters) for tool response + CLI display.\n  3) Include metadata in tool response: stdout_path, stderr_path, stdout_bytes, stderr_bytes, preview_truncated.\n  4) Preserve current UX by showing truncated preview in CLI while retaining full output on disk.\n  \n  Done when: reproducing command-heavy codex run no longer grows heap unbounded from terminal/run output, and full output is still retrievable from session artifacts.\nSpec ref:  @cli-ralph\nTags:      ralph, memory, session-log\nCreated:   2026-02-27T09:18:07.599Z\n\n─── Spec Context ───\nRalph command - automated task loop\nType: feature\nImplementation: implemented\nDescription:\n  Automated task loop using ACP protocol. Runs claude-agent-acp agent in a loop to process kspec tasks autonomously with full event logging and streaming output.\nAcceptance Criteria:\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: ready tasks exist\n    When: kspec ralph is run with --max-loops N\n    Then: spawns ACP agent and runs up to N iterations\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: no ready tasks exist\n    When: kspec ralph is run\n    Then: command exits with message indicating no ready tasks\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: a loop iteration starts\n    When: agent picks and works on a task\n    Then: agent uses task start, task note, and task complete commands per working procedure\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: a loop iteration ends with work still in progress\n    When: agent cannot complete the task in one iteration\n    Then: agent commits WIP, adds note documenting progress, and task remains in_progress for next iteration\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: a loop iteration completes (task done or WIP)\n    When: there are uncommitted changes\n    Then: agent commits the changes with appropriate message\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: --dry-run flag is provided\n    When: kspec ralph --dry-run is run\n    Then: shows the prompt that would be sent without executing agent\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: agent returns error during iteration\n    When: the error occurs\n    Then: retry the iteration up to max-retries times before failing the loop\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: multiple consecutive iterations fail after all retries\n    When: the failure count reaches max-failures threshold\n    Then: the loop exits early with an error message\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: --adapter flag is provided\n    When: kspec ralph --adapter <id> is run\n    Then: uses specified adapter (default claude-agent-acp)\n  [ac-10]\n    Given: session starts\n    When: agent spawns\n    Then: creates new session with ULID and logs session.start event\n  [ac-11]\n    Given: agent streams updates\n    When: updates arrive\n    Then: displays streaming output to CLI and logs to session events\n  [ac-12]\n    Given: prompt is sent\n    When: iteration starts\n    Then: logs prompt.sent event with full prompt content\n  [ac-13]\n    Given: session ends\n    When: loop completes or errors\n    Then: logs session.end event with status and triggers commit\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: a loop iteration starts\n    When: building prompt for the agent\n    Then: creates a fresh ACP session so each iteration has a clean context window\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: --focus flag is provided with instructions\n    When: building prompt for each iteration\n    Then: includes the focus instructions prominently in the prompt, emphasizing they apply to all iterations\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: ralph loop is running\n    When: checking for available tasks (ready or in_progress)\n    Then: only considers tasks with automation: eligible status; both ready tasks and in_progress tasks are filtered by automation eligibility\n  [ac-17]\n    Given: ralph loop is running with --restart-every N (N > 0)\n    When: iteration completes and iteration number is divisible by N\n    Then: agent process is killed and respawned to prevent memory buildup\n  [ac-18]\n    Given: --restart-every 0 is specified\n    When: iterations complete\n    Then: agent process is never restarted (maintains single agent instance)\n  [ac-19]\n    Given: ralph loop iteration completes\n    When: determining whether to continue looping\n    Then: loop continues if automation:eligible ready tasks OR automation:eligible in_progress tasks exist; exits with message when neither remain\n  [ac-20]\n    Given: processPendingReviewTasks completes during iteration\n    When: checking for loop continuation\n    Then: uses freshly gathered task context (not stale from iteration start) to detect tasks that became ready due to dependency unblocking\n  [ac-21]\n    Given: User runs kspec ralph with --tasks @ref1,@ref2\n    When: task selection runs each iteration\n    Then: only the explicitly listed tasks are considered for work, regardless of automation eligibility of other tasks; exits when all listed tasks are completed or blocked\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":965730525},"formatted_output":"Ralph: Stream terminal/run output to session files and return bounded previews\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KJF687QGPXXV00F9ZPTQJKYF\nType:      bug\nStatus:    pending\nPriority:  1\nAutomation: eligible\n\n─── Description ───\n  Problem: terminal/run currently accumulates child stdout/stderr in unbounded in-memory strings, which can OOM long codex runs.\n  \n  Scope (steps 1-2):\n  1) In terminal/run handler, stream stdout/stderr directly to per-session files (e.g., .kspec/sessions/<id>/tool-output/<toolCallId>.stdout.log and .stderr.log).\n  2) Keep only bounded in-memory preview (e.g., first N chars/lines and byte counters) for tool response + CLI display.\n  3) Include metadata in tool response: stdout_path, stderr_path, stdout_bytes, stderr_bytes, preview_truncated.\n  4) Preserve current UX by showing truncated preview in CLI while retaining full output on disk.\n  \n  Done when: reproducing command-heavy codex run no longer grows heap unbounded from terminal/run output, and full output is still retrievable from session artifacts.\nSpec ref:  @cli-ralph\nTags:      ralph, memory, session-log\nCreated:   2026-02-27T09:18:07.599Z\n\n─── Spec Context ───\nRalph command - automated task loop\nType: feature\nImplementation: implemented\nDescription:\n  Automated task loop using ACP protocol. Runs claude-agent-acp agent in a loop to process kspec tasks autonomously with full event logging and streaming output.\nAcceptance Criteria:\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: ready tasks exist\n    When: kspec ralph is run with --max-loops N\n    Then: spawns ACP agent and runs up to N iterations\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: no ready tasks exist\n    When: kspec ralph is run\n    Then: command exits with message indicating no ready tasks\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: a loop iteration starts\n    When: agent picks and works on a task\n    Then: agent uses task start, task note, and task complete commands per working procedure\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: a loop iteration ends with work still in progress\n    When: agent cannot complete the task in one iteration\n    Then: agent commits WIP, adds note documenting progress, and task remains in_progress for next iteration\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: a loop iteration completes (task done or WIP)\n    When: there are uncommitted changes\n    Then: agent commits the changes with appropriate message\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: --dry-run flag is provided\n    When: kspec ralph --dry-run is run\n    Then: shows the prompt that would be sent without executing agent\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: agent returns error during iteration\n    When: the error occurs\n    Then: retry the iteration up to max-retries times before failing the loop\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: multiple consecutive iterations fail after all retries\n    When: the failure count reaches max-failures threshold\n    Then: the loop exits early with an error message\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: --adapter flag is provided\n    When: kspec ralph --adapter <id> is run\n    Then: uses specified adapter (default claude-agent-acp)\n  [ac-10]\n    Given: session starts\n    When: agent spawns\n    Then: creates new session with ULID and logs session.start event\n  [ac-11]\n    Given: agent streams updates\n    When: updates arrive\n    Then: displays streaming output to CLI and logs to session events\n  [ac-12]\n    Given: prompt is sent\n    When: iteration starts\n    Then: logs prompt.sent event with full prompt content\n  [ac-13]\n    Given: session ends\n    When: loop completes or errors\n    Then: logs session.end event with status and triggers commit\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: a loop iteration starts\n    When: building prompt for the agent\n    Then: creates a fresh ACP session so each iteration has a clean context window\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: --focus flag is provided with instructions\n    When: building prompt for each iteration\n    Then: includes the focus instructions prominently in the prompt, emphasizing they apply to all iterations\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: ralph loop is running\n    When: checking for available tasks (ready or in_progress)\n    Then: only considers tasks with automation: eligible status; both ready tasks and in_progress tasks are filtered by automation eligibility\n  [ac-17]\n    Given: ralph loop is running with --restart-every N (N > 0)\n    When: iteration completes and iteration number is divisible by N\n    Then: agent process is killed and respawned to prevent memory buildup\n  [ac-18]\n    Given: --restart-every 0 is specified\n    When: iterations complete\n    Then: agent process is never restarted (maintains single agent instance)\n  [ac-19]\n    Given: ralph loop iteration completes\n    When: determining whether to continue looping\n    Then: loop continues if automation:eligible ready tasks OR automation:eligible in_progress tasks exist; exits with message when neither remain\n  [ac-20]\n    Given: processPendingReviewTasks completes during iteration\n    When: checking for loop continuation\n    Then: uses freshly gathered task context (not stale from iteration start) to detect tasks that became ready due to dependency unblocking\n  [ac-21]\n    Given: User runs kspec ralph with --tasks @ref1,@ref2\n    When: task selection runs each iteration\n    Then: only the explicitly listed tasks are considered for work, regardless of automation eligibility of other tasks; exits when all listed tasks are completed or blocked\n","status":"completed"}